## Overview

ref: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/29535#issuecomment-6017306253

My analysis is that views of host-buffer tensors can end up assigned into the meta backend splits. This usually happens when we perform some reshape of the extracted token embeddings before using them:

```c++
// for example, something like this
// embd is typically placed in a host buffer
embd = ggml_get_rows(model.token_embd, ids);

// ... other ops can optionally go here ...

embd = ggml_reshape_3d(embd, x, y, z);
res = ggml_mul_mat(model.w, embd);
```

I tried to modify the scheduler to prevent that (i.e. always keep the reshapes/views in the host split), but it gets a bit tricky since we don't have a guarantee where the reshapes/views nodes will end up in the graph - they are not always arranged next to the host ops (GET_ROWS in this case) depending on what other ops are performed before the `res` computation.

I don't see a reason why the meta backend cannot just ignore these nodes. After all, they don't cause any problem with other backends, so it seems something that should be fixed in the Meta backend. There is already a related FIXME comment. This PR extends the logic to handle this.

## Additional information

The K2 Horizon model can now be used with `-sm tensor`. This is also helps with a follow-up refactoring in #30160 .

